kevin: I can extract a minimal retry helper for JS + Python. My proposal: show the SDK's built-in retry first, then an optional tiny wrapper. Minimal JS example below:
```js
// JS custom backoff wrapper (minimal, for docs)
async function withBackoff(fn, retries = 3) {
  let delay = 200;
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (e) {
      if (i === retries - 1) throw e;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));
      delay *= 2;
    }
  }
}
```

